{"url": "https://www.umsl.edu/gradschool/funding/graduatetuition.html", "final_url": "https://www.umsl.edu/gradschool/funding/graduatetuition.html", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-11-14", "text": "Graduate Tuition | UMSL\nSkip to Main Content\nUniversity ofMissouri\u2013St. Louis\nApply\nRequest Info\nGive\nGraduate School\nGraduate School Policies\nGraduate School Home\nAbout the Graduate School\nContact Us\nProspective Students\nProspective Students Home\nHow to Apply\nAdmissions FAQs\nApplication Fee\nAdmitted Students\nGraduate Programs\nPrograms Home\nDoctoral\nMasters\nSpecialist\nCertificates\nNon-degree\nLifelong Learner\nAccelerated Masters\nFunding Grad School\nFunding Grad School Home\nGraduate Tuition\nAssistantships\nTravel Support\nExternal Funding\nCurrent Students\nCurrent Student Information\nGraduation Deadlines\nGraduate Student Handbook\nOral Defense Announcements\nThree Minute Thesis\nGraduate Research Fair\nFaculty\nFaculty Information\nGraduate Program Directors\nGraduate Council\nAdvisors\nForms\nCurrent Page:\nGraduate Tuition\nGraduate School\nGraduate School Policies\nGraduate School Home\nAbout the Graduate School\nContact Us\nProspective Students\nProspective Students Home\nHow to Apply\nAdmissions FAQs\nApplication Fee\nAdmitted Students\nGraduate Programs\nPrograms Home\nDoctoral\nMasters\nSpecialist\nCertificates\nNon-degree\nLifelong Learner\nAccelerated Masters\nFunding Grad School\nFunding Grad School Home\nGraduate Tuition\nAssistantships\nTravel Support\nExternal Funding\nCurrent Students\nCurrent Student Information\nGraduation Deadlines\nGraduate Student Handbook\nOral Defense Announcements\nThree Minute Thesis\nGraduate Research Fair\nFaculty\nFaculty Information\nGraduate Program Directors\nGraduate Council\nAdvisors\nForms\nGraduate Tuition\nGraduate School\nFunding Opportunities\nGraduate Tuition\nThere are so many reasons to chose UMSL, and our graduate tuition value is one of them. Both Missouri and Illinois residents qualify for graduate in-state tuition, and residents of other states may qualify for reduced rates as well.\nFollow the links below to see what goes into calculating a graduate student's tuition & fees.\nTuition and Fees\nThe Student Financial Services Office provides extensive information about tuition & fee rates for each fiscal year. Applicants can calculate a quick, general estimate of tuition and fees by using the Fee Estimator!\nInternational Admissions\nApplicants that have international transcripts are processed by the UMSL Global Office. International applicants are encouraged to reach out to the UMSL Global Office with questions related to Non-Resident tuition, assessments (such as TOEFL), visas & immigration, and priority deadlines.\nResidency Information\nThis link walks applicants through the residency requirements that must be satisfied for them to be classified as a Resident for Fee Purposes.\nMidwest Student Exchange Program\nThis program makes out-of-state tuition more affordable for students from several Midwestern states.\nMetropolitan Rate Program (for Illinois Residents)\nThis program allows Illinois residents access to in-state tuition.\nGraduate School\nOne University Blvd., 121 Woods Hall\nSt. Louis, MO 63121-4400\nOffice Number:\n(314) 516-5900\nGraduate Admissions:\n(314) 516-5458\n\u00a9\nThe Curators of the University of Missouri |\nAccessibility |\nDMCA Policy |\nPrivacy Policy |\nCareers at UMSL\nUMSL is an equal opportunity employer. For more information, visit our UMSL Statement of Nondiscrimination.\nUniversity of\nMissouri\u2013St. Louis\nApply\nRequest Info\nGive\nAdmissions\nVisit UMSL\nAdmissions\nFinancial Aid\nResidential Life\nNew Student Programs\nAdvanced Credit Program\nAcademics\nMajors and Degrees\nResearch\nColleges and Schools\nLibraries\nCourse Schedule\nOnline Programs\nAdvanced Workforce Center\nCampus Life\nStudent Involvement\nVeterans Center\nCareer Services\nHealth, Counseling, Disability Access\n